{"id": "EUVD-2026-81807", "enisaUuid": "15673bf1-a033-3c1a-ada4-125c369e6c97", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: xilinx: formatter_pcm: fix stream_data leak on open error\n\nIn xlnx_formatter_pcm_open(), stream_data is allocated and\nadata->play_stream or adata->capture_stream is assigned early.  If a\nlater step, such as snd_pcm_hw_constraint_step() or\nsnd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer(), fails, the function returns the error\nimmediately.  ALSA does not call the close callback when open fails, so\nstream_data is leaked and the stream pointer is left dangling, pointing\nto a substream that ALSA frees.  A later interrupt would then call\nsnd_pcm_period_elapsed() on the freed substream.\n\nFree stream_data and clear the stream pointer on the error paths.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e1a2d9fff57f3a2b1a0f54d128d64245a253004", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edf81b293cba1b00a5e71becf184414f6991a6ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fd89a51b8cfe788df67f54b716b305dd45b8468", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c38ae4a465691947977c25d10394da22a64a19f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9030aa4e14b704dc39ee208207cb65064020d857", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b30628dfc2b2fad3b55a9441776a226035045fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e0ce77df7d9808926719d7950a07fbad14ea9ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b992511180e126150c6ad3580a6fd568c385f4c6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90214", "GHSA-2gxq-r2mx-5g9g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "090f259f-d942-3fc7-b63d-6ee2530734ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "0e18de06-6ecb-3221-9255-13b80084dce7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <5e1a2d9fff57f3a2b1a0f54d128d64245a253004"}, {"id": "1033a9a9-7ed8-3d44-bbb2-98dc11b4feca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "2271b20e-f4fa-3f29-a711-e0b6bb429fda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <edf81b293cba1b00a5e71becf184414f6991a6ca"}, {"id": "270dde06-941b-39b3-a55c-304ff7f6334a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "46cceba7-6ff0-30a6-bf6d-203fe5fb6cda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <9030aa4e14b704dc39ee208207cb65064020d857"}, {"id": "5ba61ecd-0764-3ee6-93fa-f214eccd5737", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5fe6cc84-edf2-346e-9262-b5cddd921f19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6b11ce23-0f69-3aa7-a1a8-b5e651ed39c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "6fd5bef1-95b0-307c-9dcf-ac5c366a3962", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <8c38ae4a465691947977c25d10394da22a64a19f"}, {"id": "87416ba6-5274-3cce-bfa3-18c14914ea01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <b992511180e126150c6ad3580a6fd568c385f4c6"}, {"id": "8dc018dd-04f5-342a-a126-6661df237735", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "927bcd9e-fc4d-3584-ad4b-9c88df69e048", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6f6c3c36f0917be24587eeba818ab4fdfcb5465a <4e0ce77df7d9808926719d7950a07fbad14ea9ef"}, {"id": "ad8a78fc-c892-3b3d-86a3-aa7b4598478e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"nam